{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 7,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.671,
            0.049,
            0.846,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Finding the Unknown"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.088,
            0.772,
            0.126
          ],
          "content": "Can we check that $x = { \\frac { 1 1 } { 5 } }$ is the correct solution to the equation?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.132,
            0.846,
            0.185
          ],
          "content": "We can check this by substituting x with the value $\\frac { 1 1 } { 5 }$ in the equation $5x - 4 = 7$ , and checking if the $\\mathrm{LHS} = \\mathrm{RHS}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.186,
            0.551,
            0.222
          ],
          "content": "Substituting x with $\\frac { 1 1 } { 5 }$ in the LHS we get,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.434,
            0.22,
            0.594,
            0.348
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned} \\mathrm{LHS} &= 5\\left(\\frac{11}{5}\\right) - 4 \\\\&= \\mathrm{ 必 }\\left(\\frac{11}{5}\\right) - 4 \\\\&= 11 - 4 \\\\&= 7\\\\ \\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_7_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.354,
            0.425,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": "This is the same as the RHS."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.38,
            0.657,
            0.416
          ],
          "content": "So, $\\frac { 1 1 } { 5 }$ is indeed the correct solution to the equation."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.422,
            0.6,
            0.445
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Example 5: Solve the equation 11y $+(-5)=61$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.448,
            0.847,
            0.487
          ],
          "content": "To retain only the unknown term 11y on one side, we need to remove the term –5. This can be done by subtracting (–5) from both sides."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.369,
            0.486,
            0.628,
            0.507
          ],
          "content": "11y+(-5)-(-5)=61-(-5).",
          "image_source": "images/page_7_equation_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.511,
            0.23,
            0.53
          ],
          "content": "That is,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.452,
            0.535,
            0.546,
            0.555
          ],
          "content": "11y = 66.",
          "image_source": "images/page_7_equation_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.558,
            0.718,
            0.579
          ],
          "content": "We can directly find the value of y, seeing that $11 \\times 6 = 66$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.583,
            0.588,
            0.603
          ],
          "content": "We can also divide both sides by 11 to find y."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.411,
            0.607,
            0.586,
            0.628
          ],
          "content": "11y \\div 11 = 66 \\div 11.",
          "image_source": "images/page_7_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.631,
            0.667,
            0.652
          ],
          "content": "So $y = 6$ is the solution to the equation 11y $r + ( - 5 ) = 6 1$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.656,
            0.572,
            0.676
          ],
          "content": "Can you check that this solution is correct?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.689,
            0.48,
            0.713
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Example 6: Solve $6y + 7 = 4y + 21$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.715,
            0.786,
            0.736
          ],
          "content": "In this equation, expressions with an unknown are on both sides."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.749,
            0.846,
            0.79
          ],
          "content": "？ We have seen how to solve equations when the unknown term is on one side. What can be done to bring the unknown terms to the same side?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.795,
            0.554,
            0.815
          ],
          "content": "Subtracting 4y from both sides, we get"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.377,
            0.814,
            0.62,
            0.834
          ],
          "content": "6y+7-4y=4y+21-4y.",
          "image_source": "images/page_7_equation_21.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.839,
            0.211,
            0.857
          ],
          "content": "So,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.443,
            0.857,
            0.555,
            0.877
          ],
          "content": "2 y + 7 = 2 1 .",
          "image_source": "images/page_7_equation_23.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.807,
            0.933,
            0.843,
            0.95
          ],
          "content": "171"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
